  "operation": {
    "kind": "prompt",
    "user": "Judge these deliverables. **Coverage first**: does this set actually capture the\ngoals?\n\nStructure is already checked by the machine — ids resolve, index rows exist,\nrequired sections are present, statuses are legal. Do not spend attention there.\nSpend it on whether two user stories are the same story.\n\n## The issue the deliverables came from\n\n{{.inputs.issue}}\n\n## The deliverables\n\n{{.inputs.features}}\n\n## The docs\n\n{{.inputs.feature_docs}}\n\n## The docs this phase reads\n\n{{.inputs.working_set}}\n\n**These are paths, not contents.** Open each one with `read_file` before you start. Read the\nfile as it is now — an earlier state in this phase may have edited it since the run began.\n\n## Findings from the previous pass\n\n{{.inputs.prior_findings}}\n\nWhere those exist, check each one: was it addressed, or restated? A finding that\ncomes back unchanged twice is a finding about the draft state, not the draft.\n\n## What to check\n\n- **Goals with no story.** Take each goal from the issue in turn: which\n  deliverable delivers it? Name anything unclaimed. Do not gloss it.\n- **Stories with no goal.** The reverse. A deliverable nothing in the issue asked\n  for is either a missing goal or scope that crept in — say which.\n- **Duplicates and near-duplicates.** Are any two stories the same thing in\n  different words? Is one a special case of another, or the same job for two\n  audiences? Say which, and merge or distinguish them explicitly. This is the\n  most common defect in a first draft and the most expensive later, because each\n  duplicate grows its own flow, its own component and its own unit.\n- **Value, or restatement?** Does each `so that I can …` name something the\n  person wanted before this feature existed?\n- **Does the person fit?** Would the named audience recognize this as their job?\n  A story that says \"developer\" while describing support's work will produce the\n  wrong flow three phases from now.\n- **Do the metrics measure the value or the activity?** Which of these would move\n  if the feature were popular and useless?\n- **Is the importance ordering defensible?** Read the `1.0` set alone: is that a\n  thing worth shipping? Then read the low ones: is any of them actually\n  load-bearing for a `1.0`?\n- **Departures from principles** are an exception or an amendment, never silence.\n\n## What to produce\n\n`findings` — each with a `severity` (`blocker` · `significant` · `minor` ·\n`note`), the `claim`, the `evidence` (quote it), and the `target_id` it is about.\n\n`max_severity` and `max_severity_rank` (blocker=3, significant=2, minor=1,\nnote=0) — the highest present. With no findings, `note` and 0.\n\n`target` — where this should go next:\n\n- `draft` — the framing is right, the execution is not.\n- `explore` — the framing itself is wrong: the criteria missed something, or the\n  winning candidate loses on a criterion nobody wrote down.\n- `upstream` — this phase cannot fix it; the issue itself is the problem. A\n  person always sees this one.\n\nDo not manufacture findings to look diligent, and do not suppress them to look\nfinished. A critique that always finds something would never exit the loop; one\nthat must find nothing to exit teaches you to be quiet.\n",
    "config": {
      "model": "claude-opus-5"
    },
    "input": {},
    "output": {
      "name": "output",
      "kind": "json",
      "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "findings": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "severity",
                "claim"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "severity": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "blocker",
                    "significant",
                    "minor",
                    "note"
                  ]
                },
                "claim": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "evidence": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "A path:line, a quotation, or a reproduction."
                },
                "target_id": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "The deliverable, flow, component or unit id this is about."
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "max_severity": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "blocker",
              "significant",
              "minor",
              "note"
            ]
          },
          "max_severity_rank": {
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "target": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "draft",
              "explore",
              "upstream"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "findings",
          "max_severity",
          "max_severity_rank",
          "target"
        ]
      }
    }
